## CODE AUDIT: Net Savings Calculation

**metrics.go:374-379** — netSavings derivation:
```go
income := ts.FilterByType(models.Income)
outflows := ts.FilterByType(models.Outflow)

totalIncome := income.SumAmount()
totalExpenses := math.Abs(outflows.SumAmount())
netSavings := totalIncome - totalExpenses
```

✓ Formula: `netSavings = totalIncome - totalExpenses`
✓ Expense basis: `math.Abs(outflows.SumAmount())` where `outflows := ts.FilterByType(models.Outflow)`

**transaction.go:17-26** — TransactionType enum:
```go
const (
    Income  TransactionType = "Income"
    Outflow TransactionType = "Outflow"
    Transfer TransactionType = "Transfer"  // distinct type, not Outflow
)
// Comment: "a Transfer row falls out of Total aggregation"
```

✓ Transfer is DISTINCT from Outflow
✓ FilterByType(Outflow) EXCLUDES transfers by design

**metrics.go:370-372** (plan-exclusion note):
```
TotalIncome/TotalExpenses/NetSavings are computed above this point,
from the FULL outflow set, and are untouched -- they reflect every
dollar actually spent regardless of the flag
```

✓ One-time/flagged expenses are included (no distinct TransactionType for one-time)

